        "id": "R01",
        "item": "G02",
        "problem": "Azure platform virtual address 168.63.129.16 is globally unicast but is not an ordinary public destination; exclude it in the public-only policy. Explicit CIDR allowlists remain intentional opt-in.",
        "source": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/what-is-ip-address-168-63-129-16",
        "status": "corrected and verified"
      },
      {
        "id": "R02",
        "item": "G04",
        "problem": "Incomplete migrations did not check for missing prerequisite history during status or reconciliation.",
        "correction": "Shared prerequisite-history inspection blocks reconciliation and ready-step resume; protocol regression simulates history loss without touching real database data.",
        "status": "corrected and verified"
      },
      {
        "id": "R03",
        "item": "G03",
        "problem": "The verifier formatter originally redacted pointers only; formatting a copied value could expose decoded key bytes.",
        "correction": "Value-receiver formatting protects both pointers and values; all ordinary formatting verbs are asserted to return only the fixed redacted label.",
        "status": "corrected and verified"
      },
      {
        "id": "R04",
        "item": "G03",
        "problem": "Stripe timestamp duplication was detected by nonempty value rather than presence, accepting a valid signature after an empty first t field.",
        "correction": "Track timestamp presence independently; reject repeated timestamps including empty values. Add regression permutations and a Stripe parser fuzz target seeded with the valid-signature edge case.",
        "status": "corrected and verified"
      }
    ],
    "observations": [
      "Cookie no-store defaults preserve existing downstream override ownership; ETag integration regression passes.",
